  "protocol_notes": [
    "both emulators start from power-on with the same controller bytes; nes-py's RAM is all zeros at power-on and the tracer is given the same",
    "nes-py's processor-status byte has its bits in the reverse order (CPU_Flags in nes_py/nes/include/cpu_opcodes.hpp); it is translated before comparison, and a status byte pushed on the stack legitimately differs between the two",
    "the six timing-dependent wait loops are removed from both instruction streams before comparison and reported separately"
  ],
